CHAPTER II

SPECIAL PROVISIONS FOR THE APPLICATION OF ACT IN CERTAIN CASES

16. Persons to be attested. The following persons shall be attested, namely :
(a) all persons enrolled as combatants ;
(b) all other persons subject to this Act as may be prescribed by the Federal Government.

24. Power to modify certain fundamental rights in their application to persons subject to this Act. Subject to the provisions of any law for the time being in force relating to the Air Force or to any branch thereof, the Federal Government may, by notification, make rules2restricting in such manner and to such extent as may be specified the right of any person subject to this Act

(a) to be a member of, or to be associated in any way with, any trade union or labour union, or any class of trade or labour union or any society, institution or association, or any class of societies, institutions or associations ;

(b) to attend or address any meeting or to take part in any demonstration organized by anybody of persons for any political or other purposes ;

(c) to communicate with the press or to publish or cause to be published any book, letter or other document.

