86. Punishment of officers and warrant officers. An officer having power to convene a general court‑martial or such other officer as is, with the consent of the Federal Government specified by the Chief of the Air Staff may, in the prescribed manner, proceed against an officer below the rank of wing commander or a warrant officer, who is charged with an offence under this Act, and award one or more of the following punishments, that is to say :

